  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🌋 Dunmer Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Dark elf names from Morrowind to Skyrim: a sharp first name, a family name and, if you like, a Great House."
    },
    "intro": "Dunmer names are short, sharp and full of v, r and l sounds: Revyn Sadri, the trader in Windhelm; Brelyna Maryon at the College of Winterhold; Teldryn Sero, the sellsword on Solstheim. This **Dunmer name generator** builds names in that style, a first name and a family name, and can add one of Morrowind's Great Houses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How Dunmer names work",
        "content": "<p>Most Dunmer in the games have a first name and a family name. In Skyrim you'll meet <strong>Revyn Sadri</strong> and <strong>Aval Atheron</strong> in Windhelm, <strong>Drevis Neloren</strong> and <strong>Brelyna Maryon</strong> at the College of Winterhold, and <strong>Ambarys Rendar</strong> running the New Gnisis Cornerclub.</p><p>Some important Dunmer go by one name. <strong>Neloth</strong>, the Telvanni <a href=\"wizard-name-generator.html\">wizard</a> on Solstheim, is the best-known example. The Ashlanders, the nomadic tribes of Morrowind's wastes, keep their own traditions too.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "The Great Houses",
        "content": "<p>Dunmer society in Morrowind was organised around Great Houses. The ones you meet most often are:</p><ul><li><strong>House Redoran:</strong> warriors, devoted to duty and honour.</li><li><strong>House Hlaalu:</strong> traders and politicians, comfortable with the Empire.</li><li><strong>House Telvanni:</strong> powerful, reclusive wizards like Neloth.</li></ul><p>House Indoril and House Dres were Great Houses too. The <em>With a Great House</em> format adds a house to the name. It's a quick way to give a character a background: a Redoran and a Telvanni would not get on.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What the names sound like",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Male first names</strong> often end in <em>-yn</em>, <em>-ys</em> or <em>-as</em>: Revyn, Ambarys, Drevis. Short and clipped.</li><li><strong>Female first names</strong> usually end in <em>-a</em> or <em>-i</em>: Brelyna, Ravyna, Malsi.</li><li><strong>Family names</strong> are two or three syllables, often ending in <em>-en</em>, <em>-on</em> or <em>-i</em>: Sadri, Atheron, Neloren.</li></ul><p>All the names in this generator are new, so your character won't share a name with one from the games.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Do Dunmer have last names?",
        "answer": "Most do: Revyn Sadri, Brelyna Maryon and Teldryn Sero in Skyrim all have a first and family name. Some, like the wizard Neloth, go by one name."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are the Dunmer Great Houses?",
        "answer": "The political houses of Morrowind. The best-known are Redoran (warriors), Hlaalu (traders) and Telvanni (wizards); Indoril and Dres were Great Houses too."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are Dunmer the same as D&D drow?",
        "answer": "Both are <a href=\"dark-elf-name-generator.html\">dark elves</a>, but they're different peoples from different worlds. For D&D drow, see the <a href=\"baldurs-gate-3-name-generator.html\">Baldur's Gate 3</a> and Dark Elf name generators."
      }
    ]
